      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(gateway): include produced messageId on chat final/aborted events",
        "body": "## What\n\nAdds an optional, stable `messageId` to the Gateway `final` and `aborted` chat events, carrying the transcript id of the assistant message the run produced.\n\nCloses #105593.\n\n## Why\n\nToday `final` carries only `runId`, `sessionKey`, `state` — nothing about *what* the run produced. External clients (e.g. the Open WebUI pipe) have to re-fetch the transcript and guess \"the last assistant message\", which is decoupled from the run and causes duplicate proactive deliveries: a background run (heartbeat/sub-agent/yield) ends with a contentless `final`, the client re-ships the transcript tail under a new `runId`, and the same message gets persisted twice.\n\nWith `messageId` on the event, clients can dedup on `(sessionKey, messageId)` deterministically.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `packages/gateway-protocol`: add optional `messageId` to `ChatFinalEventSchema` and `ChatAbortedEventSchema` (`additionalProperties: false` preserved).\n- `src/gateway/server-chat.ts`: thread the produced `messageId` through the agent-event handler onto the emitted final/aborted payload.\n- `src/gateway/server-methods/chat.ts`: populate `messageId` from the appended message on the synchronous final payload.\n- Tests in `server.agent.gateway-server-agent-b.test.ts`.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nFully additive and backward-compatible — the field is optional; existing clients that ignore it are unaffected.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Rebased on latest `main`.\n- Targeted gateway tests pass locally (`server.agent.gateway-server-agent-b.test.ts` + sibling shard: 32/32). Full repo typecheck/test left to CI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
